Reports merged into #4471 need to be separated by cause. The exported classifier distinguishes
a shared date parser from a booking-form hint mismatch; a matching subject does not establish
a shared cause. The table counts each report ID once, even when export pages overlap.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What we report

**Parser.** The shared parser reads dates month first, while day-first tenants write the day
first. This can swap the intended day and month. Assignment requires a day-first tenant and
an app/email report or a booking-v2 form report. App/email reports from booking-v3 tenants
also belong here; the form-hint condition below applies only to the form channel.

<p>{#if issues.parser.url}<a href={issues.parser.url}>Parser issue: shared month-first date interpretation</a>{:else}Parser issue not yet published. The <a href="../delivery/issues/parser.md">local parser issue draft</a> is ready for review.{/if}</p>

**Hint.** Booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while its form interprets the date in the
tenant's day-first order. Following the displayed hint can therefore produce the wrong date.
Assignment requires a day-first tenant, the form channel and booking-v3's month-first hint.
The hint and the form's interpretation need to agree.

<p>{#if issues.hint.url}<a href={issues.hint.url}>Hint issue: booking-v3 date guidance and interpretation disagree</a>{:else}Hint issue not yet published. The <a href="../delivery/issues/hint.md">local hint issue draft</a> is ready for review.{/if}</p>

Intake tags are guesses based on the reporter's browser. The table shows tags within each
computed cause, including disagreements. Tenant locale, tenant form and report channel
determine assignment; subject, browser locale and intake tag do not.

<Callout kind="warn">
The desk-note reports footnoted under the table remain counted once in the parser group.
Their wording includes one-day differences, a June-only shift and an invite arriving before
booking. Those symptoms need further investigation: they do not establish a timezone defect
or another cause. The export provides classification evidence, not a verified production fix.
</Callout>

## Incoming reports and merges

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The received series groups reports by `receivedAt`, when they reached the desk. The merged
series groups them by `mergedAt`, when they were attached to the ticket. A merge spike can
collect older reports; it is not evidence of a matching spike in new arrivals. For example,
R-41200 was received on 2026-04-01 and merged on 2026-07-02.

## Basis of this review

The original exported components compute the counts, date ranges, tenant totals, tags,
footnote and timeline above. These local source files accompany this standalone HTML.
Repository: [BMachnik/mega-s01e03](https://github.com/BMachnik/mega-s01e03).

